  "id": "preview-kickoff-right",
  "title": "PREVIEW — Right kickoff: watch, then learn",
  "description": "Watch the kickoff, then replay the right-side break with a deep wide run, two runners inside the posts, and clear cross, cutback, or support options.",
  "tags": [
    "preview",
    "kickoff",
    "8v8",
    "right",
    "teaching replay"
  ],
  "notes": "FIRST PASS: Watch the kickoff flow without teaching overlays. The striker lays the ball back, the CAM releases the RM early, and the team moves forward together.\n\nSECOND PASS: Field thirds and lanes make the timing visible. The RM drives close to the end line. ST #9 attacks inside the near post and LM #11 attacks the far-post channel, so both can finish a cross.\n\nFINAL DECISION: CAM #10 holds near the edge of the central attacking lane for the cutback. RD #2 advances behind the RM as the safer support pass and can cross if the ball is recycled. Dashed routes show the three choices: cut back to 10, use 2, or cross toward 9 and 11.\n\nSETUP: Attack left to right on the 60 × 40 m 8v8 pitch. The right side is the bottom touchline. Pair this drill with the mirrored left-side kickoff.",
  "themeColor": "#2563eb",
  "pitch": "8v8",
